  "description": "BEPHIR crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C84 H100 Gd4 N10 O24 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),4(C2 H3 N1),5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd1F (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2F (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.580-3.899 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.21-110.05°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4L2(HL)2(μ3-OH)2(NO3)2](NO3)2·4CH3CN·5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
